# What the M16 demo must show, in order: the aarch64 image boots to IEx on
# qemu-system-aarch64's virt machine, the box reports its architecture, a
# module defined at the prompt survives a power cycle, and it powers off.
elixos-shim: pid 1, version
iex(1)> IEx.configure(colors: [enabled: false])
iex(2)> Elixos.info().arch
"aarch64"
iex(3)> (defmodule Demo.Arm do
iex(4)> Elixos.save()
{:ok,
elixos-shim: shutdown poweroff
iex(1)> IEx.configure(colors: [enabled: false])
iex(2)> Demo.Arm.value()
:arm_ok
elixos-shim: shutdown poweroff
